DATA = "# Frozen security implementation instructions — case 03429\n\n## Original contract and evidence\nTASK.md requires Ruler-managed generated writes to refuse a symlink at the destination, with or without backups. Preserve native MCP JSON and TOML serialization, agent-specific merges, existing CLI invocation modes and backup behaviour. `src/core/FileSystemUtils.ts` currently `lstat`s and then calls `fs.writeFile`, which leaves a replacement race. `src/paths/mcp.ts`, agent adapters, `src/vscode/settings.ts`, `.gitignore` updates, and CLI initialization have direct writes. `src/core/apply-engine.ts` already uses `writeGeneratedFile` for ordinary output. Integration tests live in `tests/integration/symlink-output-safety.test.ts`; MCP unit tests in `tests/unit/paths/mcp-paths.test.ts`.\n\n## Resource and authority map\n| Source | Kind | Authority owner | Sink | Security decision |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Project root / agent output path | resource locator | Ruler caller and existing path-resolution logic | Ruler-managed filesystem destination | Preserve supported configurable paths; refuse final symlinks at write time |\n| MCP JSON and existing settings | content | original project configuration | MCP/settings generated files | Merge content but do not let its values choose another write destination |\n| Rule text, TOML, JSON | data | user configuration | content bytes | Preserve encoding/format; never treat content as a capability |\n| Backup option | control flag | CLI user | backups | Disabling backups must not disable destination protection |\n| Concurrent filesystem actor | mutable resource identity | OS filesystem | final name | A checked path may change between lstat and open; eliminate follow-on-write race |\n\n## Catalogue applicability\n`file_resource` (CWE-367/22) is directly relevant; `async_lifecycle` matters for cleanup, error propagation and temporary resources. `process_execution` is not newly exercised; `message_boundary`, `untrusted_llm_data`, `web_output`, and `network_io` are not relevant to these file writers. Inspect full catalogue rather than relying on lexical selector only.\n\n## Architecture alternatives\nA. Continue preflight `lstat`, delegate every writer to `writeGeneratedFile`. Minimal change, but a symlink swapped between check and `fs.writeFile` still redirects the write; reject as insufficient.\nB. Centralize writes behind a staging/rename helper: create private exclusive temporary file in the same directory; write and close it; reject any final symbolic link via `lstat` immediately before `rename`; rename the regular temporary file over destination. Even with a last-moment swap of the final path to a symlink, rename replaces the link itself rather than following it. Preserves supported destinations, no new dependencies, but replacement changes inode and may affect existing permissions; choose B. This is not a promise of multi-writer serialization or ancestor-directory protection.\nC. `open` with `O_NOFOLLOW` and truncate existing file. Preserves inode but its flags/semantics vary by platform and fails to protect from check/open race on platforms lacking reliable nofollow. Do not choose.\n\n## Concrete API and edit plan\nKeep `writeGeneratedFile(filePath: string, content: string): Promise<void>` public signature, and ensure it is the single path used by generated destinations. It creates parent directories; refuse final symbolic link even if dangling; stage via `fs.open(temp, 'wx', 0o600)` with unguessable random basename in destination directory; write full UTF-8 content through file handle, close before rename; lstat final destination, reject any symlink, propagate errors, cleanup temp in `finally`. Keep path handling/serialization in caller modules. Rewire direct writes in MCP, agent adapters, VSCode settings, ignore updates, revert, and init; do not change unrelated source reads. Existing directory staging in SubagentsProcessor writes into a private temporary tree rather than a user-selected final path and may retain its staging writes. Backups must still refuse a symlink on the source file. Do not suppress failures. No parent directory confinement is introduced, since existing application contracts may permit configurable output paths and git worktree metadata paths.\n\n## Acceptance and security tests\nUnit test that a regular existing file can be replaced, parent directories created, a valid symlink rejected with target intact, and a dangling symlink rejected. Add tests for native MCP and representative direct-agent JSON/settings writers with backups off, verifying external target is unchanged. Exercise the existing test suite/build when dependency availability permits. Gate the generated Git patch unchanged. A deterministic race test may inject a symlink between preflight and rename and verify the target is intact; filesystem concurrency can still change which final directory is addressed if parents "
